 I.  INTRODUCTION 
 1.  In  this  Order,  we  deny  the  joint  application  for  review  filed  by  Constellation  Communications  Holdings,  Inc.  (Constellation),  Mobile  Communications  Holdings,  Inc.  (MCHI),  and  ICO  Global 
 Communications  (Holdings)  Limited  (ICO).  1  These  parties  request  that  we  overturn  the  International  Bureau  (Bureau)  Order  that  found  Constellation's  and  MCHI's  2  GHz  Mobile-  Satellite  Service  (MSS) 
 authorizations  to  be  null  and  void  for  failure  to  satisfy  the  first  implementation  milestone.  2  The  first  milestone  requires  a  2  GHz  MSS  system  licensee  to  enter  into  a  non-  contingent  satellite  manufacturing 
 contract  within  one  year  of  authorization.  3  Milestone  requirements  promote  efficient  use  of  limited 


