 Commercial  Systems  that  provided  CTA  would  construct,  launch,  and  provide  certain  operational  services  in  return  for  commercial  use  of  50%  of  the  satellite’s  capacity.  CTA  was  not  a  Commission  licensee,  and  thus,  the  fact  that 


 the  Commission  eventually  approved  of  that  agreement  to  allow  the  launch  is  inapposite  to  the  analysis  of  whether  a  licensee  can  meet  its  milestones  by  sharing  satellites  with  another  licensee. 
